.DS_Store

# PicoDoorBell: device-local and session files
# Note: secrets.py is intentionally committed with stub values as a template.
# Real credentials replace the stubs on-device and must never be committed.
# Tier 2 state written on-device (boot counter, queue snapshots, epoch anchor).
# Runtime data, not source; each unit owns its own.
state.json
state.json.tmp
# board.py is the per-unit copy of a boards/ file, chosen per device. The
# revision templates in boards/ are committed; the active copy is not.
/board.py
# Session handover: a bootstrapping artifact regenerated from the docs each
# time, not project documentation. Kept local so it cannot drift from the
# committed docs or accidentally carry device details into the repo.
handover.md